[32.815775, "o", "> Auto routed to Grok 4.6\r\n\r\nI'll read `calc.py` and look for actual bugs, then give you three short bullets.- `subtract` adds instead of subtracting (`return a + b`).\r\n- `divide` does not guard against `b == 0`, so it raises `ZeroDivisionError`.\r\n- No type checks: non-numeric inputs fail at runtime with a generic `TypeError`.\r\n"]
